1
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:04,404
KANBARA FAMOUS DOCTOR AGENCY

2
00:00:05,538 --> 00:00:07,440
Just a minute, Ben Casey.

3
00:00:07,574 --> 00:00:09,709
I'm getting your breakfast ready now.

4
00:00:13,146 --> 00:00:16,516
Akira, good morning. I'm hungry.

5
00:00:16,616 --> 00:00:18,451
Ben Casey eats first.

6
00:00:19,786 --> 00:00:22,555
<i>Next, news from the sports world.</i>

7
00:00:22,622 --> 00:00:26,526
<i>Kiyoaki Yokkaichi, the Japanese
track star who ran the fastest</i>

8
00:00:26,626 --> 00:00:30,230
<i>100-meter this season
in the world at 9.80 seconds,</i>

9
00:00:30,296 --> 00:00:34,434
<i>has complained of pain in his right leg</i>

10
00:00:34,501 --> 00:00:38,204
<i>and returned home
from his training camp in Florida.</i>

11
00:00:38,405 --> 00:00:40,006
<i>Mr. Yokkaichi has...</i>

12
00:00:40,073 --> 00:00:42,042
I just hope he's not hurt.

13
00:00:42,108 --> 00:00:46,312
He's the first Japanese who has
a chance to win the gold in the 100.

14
00:00:46,413 --> 00:00:48,348
Here you go, Ben Casey. There.

15
00:00:48,415 --> 00:00:51,985
<i>With his time of 9.80 seconds,
he's on par with world-leading...</i>

16
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:53,086
What?

17
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,089
I wonder if you're hurt too, Ben Casey.

18
00:00:56,156 --> 00:00:58,491
- You're the one hurt, Akira.
- What?

19
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:02,128
Ben Casey won't eat two cans
in the morning.

20
00:01:02,195 --> 00:01:04,130
Oh, dear! I already fed him.

21
00:01:04,197 --> 00:01:06,733
Be careful. You're getting on in years.

22
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,703
That's pretty rude.
There's nothing wrong with being my age.

23
00:01:10,804 --> 00:01:12,472
Who said it was wrong?

24
00:01:15,041 --> 00:01:16,643
That's noodle sauce!

25
00:01:16,709 --> 00:01:18,812
See! You're one to talk! Get it together!

26
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,513
You're getting on in years too!

27
00:01:21,681 --> 00:01:23,049
I am?

28
00:01:23,116 --> 00:01:27,087
Oh, you! I take that as a compliment.

29
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:29,022
You sure have a positive outlook.

30
00:01:29,089 --> 00:01:31,591
My attitude toward life
is always positive.

31
00:01:39,365 --> 00:01:42,435
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

32
00:01:42,502 --> 00:01:44,204
Yuck!

33
00:01:44,304 --> 00:01:48,575
<i>In 2019, the ivory towers are
completely crumbling.</i>

34
00:01:48,641 --> 00:01:49,542
SURGERY DEPARTMENT

35
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:53,480
<i>Japan's university hospitals have
fallen into tremendous debt.</i>

36
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:56,116
<i>Lifesaving medical treatment</i>

37
00:01:56,182 --> 00:01:59,819
<i>has entered the era of
financial jungle law.</i>

38
00:02:00,019 --> 00:02:01,087
KAZUMA USHIO

39
00:02:01,187 --> 00:02:04,023
Let us begin this special conference.

40
00:02:04,090 --> 00:02:05,325
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

41
00:02:05,758 --> 00:02:07,694
We sure are meeting in close quarters.

42
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:10,663
This is a top-secret conference
only for a select few.

43
00:02:10,763 --> 00:02:13,800
The patient is Kiyoaki Yokkaichi,
male, age 23.

44
00:02:14,701 --> 00:02:17,370
As you know, he's Japan's track superstar.

45
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:22,442
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance
maverick doctor, who was never part of</i>

46
00:02:22,742 --> 00:02:26,546
<i>a university medical department,
showed up.</i>

47
00:02:33,887 --> 00:02:35,021
Excuse me.

48
00:02:36,222 --> 00:02:38,458
Are you a doctor here?

49
00:02:39,225 --> 00:02:40,460
Yes.

50
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:45,598
I am Kazuma Ushio's mother.

51
00:02:45,798 --> 00:02:48,034
I'm much obliged.

52
00:02:48,535 --> 00:02:49,435
Ushio?

53
00:02:49,536 --> 00:02:51,571
Look at all the damage
to the blood vessels!

54
00:02:51,638 --> 00:02:54,307
Was this also the instructions of the AI?

55
00:02:57,477 --> 00:02:59,279
That terrible surgeon?

56
00:02:59,445 --> 00:03:03,349
Is Kazuma really that bad at surgery?

57
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:06,553
He's absolutely terrible.

58
00:03:06,886 --> 00:03:08,955
I'm terribly sorry
for the trouble he's caused.

59
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:09,856
It's okay.

60
00:03:09,923 --> 00:03:12,492
Here. These are Welsh onions
from my garden.

61
00:03:12,559 --> 00:03:14,794
They're juicy and delicious.

62
00:03:15,061 --> 00:03:17,597
- As a token of apology.
- Thanks.

63
00:03:17,664 --> 00:03:19,165
You're welcome. Goodbye.

64
00:03:28,241 --> 00:03:29,776
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA

65
00:03:29,842 --> 00:03:34,347
It's time for the conference,
but why isn't anyone here?

66
00:03:34,414 --> 00:03:36,616
That is odd. They must all be busy.

67
00:03:39,385 --> 00:03:42,388
Oh, the conference is here, right?

68
00:03:42,655 --> 00:03:44,390
That's what I heard.

69
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:52,732
Have you been frozen out?

70
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:54,667
What does "frozen out" mean?

71
00:03:54,734 --> 00:03:59,639
It means being excluded
or ostracized from the group.

72
00:03:59,739 --> 00:04:01,307
- Me too?
- I guess so.

73
00:04:02,609 --> 00:04:04,744
Seriously?

74
00:04:07,146 --> 00:04:08,214
What's the diagnosis?

75
00:04:10,216 --> 00:04:14,687
<i>The diagnosis is synovial sarcoma
of the knee, stage three.</i>

76
00:04:15,054 --> 00:04:18,157
<i>There is a five-centimeter tumor
in the right knee.</i>

77
00:04:18,324 --> 00:04:21,728
<i>There is possible infiltration
into the cartilage.</i>

78
00:04:21,794 --> 00:04:23,596
Yokkaichi has cancer?

79
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:28,301
This is unfair,
having a conference in a place like this!

80
00:04:29,702 --> 00:04:31,571
Who said you could come in?

81
00:04:31,771 --> 00:04:33,606
- Hey!
- You scared me!

82
00:04:33,673 --> 00:04:35,708
Why didn't you tell me about this?

83
00:04:35,775 --> 00:04:37,043
This is only for a select few.

84
00:04:37,477 --> 00:04:39,479
They said large conferences are useless.

85
00:04:39,579 --> 00:04:41,581
You mean I'm useless?

86
00:04:42,415 --> 00:04:45,318
Stage three synovial sarcoma of the knee.

87
00:04:46,419 --> 00:04:48,588
A five-centimeter tumor in the right knee.

88
00:04:48,688 --> 00:04:51,057
Possible infiltration into the cartilage.

89
00:04:53,693 --> 00:04:55,828
You and I are getting along.

90
00:04:56,162 --> 00:04:58,331
Okay, tell me the surgical method.

91
00:04:58,398 --> 00:05:00,133
Dr. Daimon, you weren't invited.

92
00:05:00,199 --> 00:05:03,603
<i>The surgical method is
a comprehensive tumor excision</i>

93
00:05:03,670 --> 00:05:05,638
<i>followed by artificial joint replacement.</i>

94
00:05:07,073 --> 00:05:09,142
If the synovial sarcoma is ignored,

95
00:05:09,242 --> 00:05:11,577
it could metastasize to organs
far away like the lungs.

96
00:05:11,644 --> 00:05:14,347
Surgery should be immediate.

97
00:05:16,382 --> 00:05:18,751
Dr. Daimon and the AI are in agreement.

98
00:05:19,018 --> 00:05:21,754
Doesn't it mean the AI has finally
caught up with Daimon?

99
00:05:22,021 --> 00:05:24,424
- I'll do this operation.
- Why you?

100
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:26,526
No matter how much you and the AI agree,

101
00:05:26,726 --> 00:05:29,228
this isn't a patient
I'd let a part-timer like you touch.

102
00:05:29,562 --> 00:05:32,699
He's a treasure of Japan,
with the world's fastest legs.

103
00:05:32,799 --> 00:05:34,801
- So?
- Don't act like that.

104
00:05:35,201 --> 00:05:38,104
That's exactly the reason why.
As the director of

105
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:41,307
Next-Generation Intelligent Surgery,
he's my patient.

106
00:05:42,408 --> 00:05:43,743
You can't be serious.

107
00:05:45,445 --> 00:05:46,779
"Surgery Department."

108
00:05:47,113 --> 00:05:49,415
I finally found it.

109
00:05:49,582 --> 00:05:51,084
Who are you?

110
00:05:52,418 --> 00:05:54,787
- Kazuma!
- Mom!

111
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:56,322
- "Mom"?
- "Mom"?

112
00:05:57,690 --> 00:06:02,595
Hello, everyone.
I am Kazuma Ushio's mother.

113
00:06:03,296 --> 00:06:06,766
I am much obliged to you.

114
00:06:07,066 --> 00:06:11,270
Here you go. These are juicy,
delicious Welsh onions.

115
00:06:12,004 --> 00:06:14,107
- Here you go.
- Stop that, Mom!

116
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:15,475
Miss, here you go.

117
00:06:17,977 --> 00:06:20,546
Ma'am, we met earlier.

118
00:06:21,814 --> 00:06:22,749
See?

119
00:06:23,383 --> 00:06:26,352
Those look like delicious Welsh onions.

120
00:06:26,519 --> 00:06:27,653
Where are they from?

121
00:06:28,087 --> 00:06:29,589
You gave them to me.

122
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:33,559
Here you are. They're delicious.

123
00:06:33,659 --> 00:06:35,661
Mom! Come with me.

124
00:06:36,195 --> 00:06:37,363
Let's go this way, Mom.

125
00:06:37,797 --> 00:06:40,233
I'm glad I met everyone. Excuse me.

126
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,135
Goodbye.

127
00:06:42,301 --> 00:06:45,138
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

128
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:48,641
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

129
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:20,173
- Okay, Mom. Here goes.
- Here goes.

130
00:07:21,207 --> 00:07:24,277
Tell me the names of these three animals.

131
00:07:24,377 --> 00:07:27,113
Repeat the following four words.

132
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:29,449
Cherry blossoms, dog...

133
00:07:29,515 --> 00:07:31,784
Count down from one hundred
in intervals of seven.

134
00:07:32,084 --> 00:07:34,687
One hundred minus seven is ninety-three.

135
00:07:34,787 --> 00:07:37,457
Ninety-three minus seven is...

136
00:07:40,493 --> 00:07:42,462
I don't know.

137
00:07:42,528 --> 00:07:48,201
- Say Mount Fuji backward.
- "Ijuf..."

138
00:07:50,036 --> 00:07:51,504
I can't do it.

139
00:07:51,571 --> 00:07:54,474
Say the words in the order
memorized from first to last.

140
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:57,577
- Elephant.
- Elephant?

141
00:08:00,446 --> 00:08:02,148
I don't remember the rest.

142
00:08:04,116 --> 00:08:05,151
What's the diagnosis?

143
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:12,024
<i>Alzheimer dementia, 85 percent.</i>

144
00:08:12,391 --> 00:08:15,595
<i>Vascular dementia, seven percent.</i>

145
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:18,531
<i>Parkinson's disease, five percent.</i>

146
00:08:18,731 --> 00:08:22,068
<i>Others, three percent.
That is my diagnosis.</i>

147
00:08:29,041 --> 00:08:31,444
The surgery department is
secretly planning

148
00:08:31,544 --> 00:08:35,047
the treatment for the track
superstar, Kiyoaki Yokkaichi.

149
00:08:35,114 --> 00:08:37,416
This VIP of VIPs is

150
00:08:37,717 --> 00:08:39,619
hospitalized here?

151
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,488
How come I don't know about it?

152
00:08:42,555 --> 00:08:44,624
I can't believe how I'm being treated.

153
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:46,425
I know how you feel.

154
00:08:46,559 --> 00:08:48,561
"Combined conferences are useless."

155
00:08:50,296 --> 00:08:52,231
"Director's rounds are useless."

156
00:08:53,599 --> 00:08:55,101
"Don't do anything."

157
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:56,769
"Sit still."

158
00:08:59,338 --> 00:09:00,339
If this is how it'll be,

159
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:04,977
then it was far better
at the detention center.

160
00:09:05,311 --> 00:09:07,280
Director, don't say things like that.

161
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:10,516
I'm just kidding.
Did you think I was serious?

162
00:09:10,983 --> 00:09:12,084
I'm sorry.

163
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:14,687
- Director.
- Yes?

164
00:09:15,187 --> 00:09:18,257
Change and...

165
00:09:18,958 --> 00:09:20,493
Never give up.

166
00:09:21,193 --> 00:09:22,395
Cut that out.

167
00:09:23,396 --> 00:09:26,132
Mom, listen to me carefully.

168
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:32,605
Mom, you have Alzheimer dementia.

169
00:09:32,705 --> 00:09:36,008
- Dementia?
- Yes.

170
00:09:37,376 --> 00:09:38,978
From now on,

171
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:44,383
this disease will slowly but surely
steal your memory.

172
00:09:45,451 --> 00:09:48,087
We can only prescribe
medication to slow the progress

173
00:09:49,155 --> 00:09:51,057
and see how it goes.

174
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:56,162
It will be just fine.

175
00:09:57,330 --> 00:10:00,333
You won't suddenly get worse
from Alzheimer's.

176
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:04,737
You can still live normally
for several years.

177
00:10:09,375 --> 00:10:11,811
I'll write a referral
for your local hospital.

178
00:10:12,778 --> 00:10:16,015
From now on, have them take care of you.

179
00:10:19,385 --> 00:10:21,120
I'm sorry.

180
00:10:23,489 --> 00:10:26,492
I've fallen ill on you.

181
00:10:31,364 --> 00:10:32,732
Dr. Ushio.

182
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:37,136
Assistant Director Tange wants you
to come to Mr. Yokkaichi's room.

183
00:10:37,203 --> 00:10:38,471
All right.

184
00:10:39,572 --> 00:10:41,107
I have to get back to work.

185
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:43,709
I'm in charge of
a very important operation.

186
00:10:44,510 --> 00:10:46,278
- I'll call you later.
- Kazuma.

187
00:10:47,079 --> 00:10:48,180
Yes?

188
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:54,120
Is it true that you're a terrible surgeon?

189
00:10:55,421 --> 00:10:58,524
- Who said that?
- Dr. Ushio, we need to hurry.

190
00:11:00,559 --> 00:11:01,727
I'll call you.

191
00:11:25,317 --> 00:11:27,153
May I talk with you a moment?

192
00:11:29,021 --> 00:11:30,122
Sure.

193
00:11:30,389 --> 00:11:35,561
He said I've got Alzheimer dementia.

194
00:11:40,232 --> 00:11:41,801
She's got Alzheimer's.

195
00:11:42,234 --> 00:11:44,136
I feel bad for Dr. Ushio.

196
00:11:44,570 --> 00:11:46,605
It's impossible to cure it.

197
00:11:49,775 --> 00:11:53,846
<i>Since he was a child,
Kazuma has been very good in school.</i>

198
00:11:55,448 --> 00:11:57,349
I'm proud of my son.

199
00:12:00,319 --> 00:12:02,555
He will continue to

200
00:12:03,089 --> 00:12:05,624
save many more patients.

201
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:11,497
He's the one thing

202
00:12:16,335 --> 00:12:17,803
I don't want to forget.

203
00:12:20,139 --> 00:12:22,308
I always want to

204
00:12:24,076 --> 00:12:25,644
watch over him.

205
00:12:31,717 --> 00:12:33,219
You probably can.

206
00:12:35,755 --> 00:12:37,656
I mean, you're still just fine.

207
00:12:40,726 --> 00:12:42,094
You're right.

208
00:12:44,130 --> 00:12:47,166
I'm glad we talked.

209
00:12:49,502 --> 00:12:51,437
Thank you.

210
00:12:57,743 --> 00:12:59,211
Take care.

211
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:22,468
I've got cancer?

212
00:13:22,535 --> 00:13:24,370
SPRINTER
KIYOAKI YOKKAICHI

213
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:26,338
- You must be kidding.
- Don't you worry.

214
00:13:26,806 --> 00:13:31,510
We, at Totei University Hospital,
stake our prestige on treating you.

215
00:13:32,444 --> 00:13:35,714
- Dr. Ushio, what is the treatment?
- Yes, sir.

216
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:40,386
The joint with the tumor will be
completely removed through surgery.

217
00:13:40,586 --> 00:13:43,389
The lost bone will be replaced
with an artificial joint.

218
00:13:44,590 --> 00:13:47,326
This was the best treatment
determined by us and the AI.

219
00:13:48,694 --> 00:13:50,830
- You want me to die?
- What?

220
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:52,264
NICHOLAS TANGE

221
00:13:52,331 --> 00:13:54,500
You're telling me I should die.

222
00:13:55,568 --> 00:13:56,569
No.

223
00:13:57,536 --> 00:14:00,539
This treatment will
save your life for sure.

224
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:02,775
It will not interfere with everyday life.

225
00:14:03,042 --> 00:14:06,378
Can I return to sprinting
with an artificial joint?

226
00:14:08,647 --> 00:14:12,718
- Unfortunately, as an athlete--
- That's what I'm talking about!

227
00:14:13,052 --> 00:14:16,088
Ending my career as a sprinter
is the same as ending my life!

228
00:14:17,223 --> 00:14:21,160
I heard this hospital has
the most advanced medical AI.

229
00:14:21,427 --> 00:14:23,796
I've also employed
the most advanced training AI

230
00:14:24,029 --> 00:14:25,431
to improve my performance.

231
00:14:25,998 --> 00:14:27,800
I trust in the power of AIs.

232
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:29,802
Nothing is impossible.

233
00:14:31,036 --> 00:14:32,805
Let me compete again in six months.

234
00:14:33,405 --> 00:14:34,640
That's impossible.

235
00:14:34,740 --> 00:14:36,575
Even with the most advanced AI,

236
00:14:36,675 --> 00:14:39,578
the kind of treatment you want
doesn't exist in today's medicine.

237
00:14:41,113 --> 00:14:44,216
Mr. Yokkaichi, I believe that
the most important of all is

238
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:48,053
- saving your life.
- In six months,

239
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:51,056
the World Track Championships
will be held in London.

240
00:14:51,824 --> 00:14:54,059
If I can't compete in that, I'm leaving.

241
00:14:54,126 --> 00:14:55,294
Mr. Yokkaichi...

242
00:14:58,697 --> 00:15:01,166
Dr. Daimon, what are you doing here?

243
00:15:01,233 --> 00:15:03,135
- Let me see his chart.
- What?

244
00:15:04,203 --> 00:15:06,372
The AI might be wrong.

245
00:15:06,772 --> 00:15:08,607
The AI could be wrong?

246
00:15:08,674 --> 00:15:10,976
- That's impossible.
- Get out!

247
00:15:11,043 --> 00:15:12,511
- Dr. Daimon--
- Hey, kid.

248
00:15:14,046 --> 00:15:17,583
If you don't have surgery, you'll die.

249
00:15:21,387 --> 00:15:23,022
Dr. Daimon!

250
00:15:28,494 --> 00:15:30,529
<i>Today, TV gossip shows had</i>

251
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:33,399
nothing but stories about Mr. Yokkaichi.

252
00:15:35,734 --> 00:15:39,638
- Let's see. Yes! <i>Riichi!</i>
- Really?

253
00:15:39,705 --> 00:15:42,274
But with synovial sarcoma,

254
00:15:42,474 --> 00:15:45,110
he'll never recover in six months.

255
00:15:49,648 --> 00:15:52,418
I know it's no good, but how's this?

256
00:15:52,518 --> 00:15:54,520
Safe!

257
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:57,556
I'll never be able to drive either.

258
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:59,124
- What?
- Drive?

259
00:15:59,491 --> 00:16:03,329
Today, I went to renew
my driver's license.

260
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:06,665
They told me to take
the cognitive performance test.

261
00:16:06,765 --> 00:16:09,368
Isn't the cognitive test
only if you're over 75?

262
00:16:09,435 --> 00:16:12,104
They thought I was over 75.

263
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:16,275
To some people, you might look over 75.
What did you do?

264
00:16:16,342 --> 00:16:19,078
I got so upset, I turned in my license.

265
00:16:19,144 --> 00:16:21,313
- Seriously?
- That's not a bad idea.

266
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:22,982
I mean, he doesn't even have a car.

267
00:16:23,048 --> 00:16:25,017
- That's right.
- Who's turn is it?

268
00:16:26,218 --> 00:16:27,619
- Wait.
- What?

269
00:16:27,686 --> 00:16:29,421
Don't you have one too many, Akira?

270
00:16:31,757 --> 00:16:33,692
You're right! That's <i>tahai!</i>

271
00:16:33,759 --> 00:16:35,260
- Sorry.
- No, you don't!

272
00:16:35,394 --> 00:16:37,162
- Returning it is a foul!
- Oh, come on!

273
00:16:37,229 --> 00:16:39,498
That's unusual for you
to commit a foul, Akira.

274
00:16:40,132 --> 00:16:43,168
- I bet you've got it.
- Got what?

275
00:16:43,235 --> 00:16:45,537
Want to give him the cognition test?

276
00:16:45,604 --> 00:16:48,173
- Let's do it.
- Okay, Mr. Kanbara,

277
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:50,576
Count down from 100 in intervals of seven.

278
00:16:50,642 --> 00:16:53,779
You underestimate me.
One hundred minus seven is ninety-three.

279
00:16:54,046 --> 00:16:58,183
- What's next?
- 86, 79, 72, 65,

280
00:16:58,250 --> 00:17:02,421
58, 51, 44, 37, 30, 23, 16, 9, 2,

281
00:17:02,521 --> 00:17:04,723
- 5, -12, -19.

282
00:17:04,957 --> 00:17:06,825
- That's so fast!
- He even went to the negatives.

283
00:17:06,892 --> 00:17:09,628
"Mount Fuji" backward is "Ijuftnuom."

284
00:17:09,728 --> 00:17:14,033
"Madam in Eden, I'm Adam" backward
is also "Madam in Eden, I'm Adam."

285
00:17:14,133 --> 00:17:17,169
"Akira Kanbara" is "Arabnak Arika."

286
00:17:17,269 --> 00:17:19,571
Okay, what's "Michiko Daimon"?

287
00:17:19,671 --> 00:17:23,475
- Okihc--
- Enough!

288
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:24,777
- Okihc--
- Enough!

289
00:17:24,843 --> 00:17:26,278
Then what's "Hiromi Jonouchi"?

290
00:17:26,578 --> 00:17:28,547
- Himi--
- Enough! I'm sorry!

291
00:17:28,647 --> 00:17:31,016
- You better believe it!
- I'm sorry.

292
00:17:35,621 --> 00:17:36,755
Mom!

293
00:17:37,756 --> 00:17:38,924
Mom!

294
00:17:39,591 --> 00:17:42,594
You came again today?
I told you to go to the local hospital.

295
00:17:43,028 --> 00:17:44,196
Did you go?

296
00:17:45,097 --> 00:17:47,266
- Well...
- What?

297
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:51,303
Who are you?

298
00:17:53,572 --> 00:17:54,807
Mom?

299
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:58,477
This is happening so fast.

300
00:18:00,112 --> 00:18:02,748
- There he is! This way!
- Doctor!

301
00:18:03,148 --> 00:18:04,483
- Doctor!
- Doctor!

302
00:18:04,716 --> 00:18:07,152
Mr. Yokkaichi is hospitalized here,
isn't he?

303
00:18:07,219 --> 00:18:08,520
Tell us his condition.

304
00:18:09,054 --> 00:18:10,589
Is it true he won't be back?

305
00:18:10,656 --> 00:18:12,291
Is his life in danger?

306
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:15,994
- I cannot comment on--
- Doctor! Give us details!

307
00:18:16,061 --> 00:18:18,464
- Doctor, please tell--
- We cannot comment on this!

308
00:18:18,564 --> 00:18:20,065
Dr. Ushio, to the director's office.

309
00:18:20,132 --> 00:18:22,501
Wait! Doctor, you have a duty to tell us!

310
00:18:22,568 --> 00:18:24,703
Please hold a press conference!

311
00:18:25,204 --> 00:18:27,339
- Please, Doctor!
- Ma'am?

312
00:18:28,173 --> 00:18:29,541
Are you all right, ma'am?

313
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:39,418
Now that the press has
gotten wind of this,

314
00:18:39,518 --> 00:18:43,789
I think we have no choice but to
hold a press conference.

315
00:18:45,090 --> 00:18:49,495
If we hold a press conference,
as the hospital director,

316
00:18:49,695 --> 00:18:52,064
I'll take care of handling it.
Leave it to me.

317
00:18:52,798 --> 00:18:55,667
We won't hold a press conference.

318
00:18:56,368 --> 00:18:58,737
- It's too risky.
- What?

319
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:01,540
In this era, any inadvertent remarks
at a press conference

320
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,542
could cause an even greater commotion.

321
00:19:04,409 --> 00:19:08,547
What's more, Mr. Yokkaichi hasn't
approved the surgery.

322
00:19:09,047 --> 00:19:10,749
Who knows what the press will say.

323
00:19:11,517 --> 00:19:13,218
I see.

324
00:19:15,187 --> 00:19:16,221
What?

325
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:21,393
Go ahead, please continue.

326
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:25,330
Dr. Ushio, how is it going
with Mr. Yokkaichi?

327
00:19:26,098 --> 00:19:27,332
Have you convinced him?

328
00:19:29,668 --> 00:19:31,603
- No, not yet.
- What's wrong with you?

329
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:33,005
That scared me!

330
00:19:33,639 --> 00:19:37,209
Totei University Hospital's Director
of Next-Generation Intelligent Surgery

331
00:19:37,442 --> 00:19:41,280
is using a diagnostic AI
to save a treasure of Japan.

332
00:19:42,014 --> 00:19:45,150
If you can't successfully complete this,
you know what will happen!

333
00:19:47,519 --> 00:19:51,156
This is far more important than

334
00:19:51,523 --> 00:19:53,559
winning a gold medal,

335
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:55,594
Dr. Ushio.

336
00:19:58,597 --> 00:19:59,798
Yes, sir.

337
00:20:05,337 --> 00:20:07,306
How's that? Do you feel better?

338
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:09,541
Yes, I'm fine.

339
00:20:11,610 --> 00:20:14,746
Ma'am, do you know where you are?

340
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:17,816
- This is a hospital, right?
- Yes, it's a hospital.

341
00:20:18,817 --> 00:20:21,019
What did you come to this hospital for?

342
00:20:24,022 --> 00:20:27,593
Oh, I remember. I came to see my son.

343
00:20:28,193 --> 00:20:31,063
- Your son is here?
- Yes. He's a doctor.

344
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:33,365
Really? What's his name?

345
00:20:33,832 --> 00:20:36,835
His name is Kazuma Ushio.

346
00:20:37,669 --> 00:20:39,504
Dr. Ushio...

347
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:44,309
But I heard he's a terrible surgeon.

348
00:20:46,144 --> 00:20:48,413
So I'm very worried about him.

349
00:20:50,349 --> 00:20:54,186
- Are you a doctor at this hospital?
- Me? Yes, I am.

350
00:20:54,519 --> 00:20:58,123
Do you happen to know where Kazuma is?

351
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:01,159
Let me see. Where could he be?

352
00:21:02,327 --> 00:21:04,663
He might be in the professor's office.

353
00:21:04,796 --> 00:21:06,632
- The professor's office?
- Yes.

354
00:21:11,069 --> 00:21:13,438
- You want to go there?
- Yes!

355
00:21:14,306 --> 00:21:16,208
- Can you get there alone?
- Yes.

356
00:21:17,209 --> 00:21:18,543
Here's how to get there.

357
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:21,780
When you leave here,
there's an elevator on the right.

358
00:21:22,014 --> 00:21:25,017
Go to the third floor and turn left
when you get off the elevator.

359
00:21:25,484 --> 00:21:27,286
When you get to the end of the hall,

360
00:21:27,352 --> 00:21:30,322
turn left,
and you'll find the professor's office.

361
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:34,559
When I leave here,
there's an elevator on the right.

362
00:21:34,626 --> 00:21:36,628
Get off at the third floor.

363
00:21:37,162 --> 00:21:39,464
I turn left when I get off,

364
00:21:40,532 --> 00:21:42,801
- End of the hall--
- At the end of the hall,

365
00:21:43,068 --> 00:21:44,670
- turn left.
- That's right.

366
00:21:44,736 --> 00:21:46,605
Okay, goodbye.

367
00:21:47,439 --> 00:21:48,774
- Take care.
- I will.

368
00:21:56,848 --> 00:21:58,684
Hey! Get out of the way!

369
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:01,086
- You're in the way!
- Hey!

370
00:22:01,386 --> 00:22:02,521
What's wrong with you?

371
00:22:10,562 --> 00:22:13,298
When I get off the elevator
on the third floor,

372
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:17,235
turn left.

373
00:22:30,716 --> 00:22:32,384
Hey! What are you doing?

374
00:22:33,552 --> 00:22:34,786
Are you playing hide and seek?

375
00:22:34,853 --> 00:22:37,122
- Yes, something like that.
- What?

376
00:22:37,656 --> 00:22:39,725
Now Demon's wandering around the hospital.

377
00:22:43,829 --> 00:22:45,263
At the end of the hall,

378
00:22:46,431 --> 00:22:47,699
turn left.

379
00:23:00,112 --> 00:23:01,113
You moron!

380
00:23:01,446 --> 00:23:02,414
That hurt!

381
00:23:07,285 --> 00:23:09,154
I finally made it.

382
00:23:09,654 --> 00:23:10,989
This is the place.

383
00:23:30,275 --> 00:23:31,743
Ma'am!

384
00:23:33,245 --> 00:23:37,616
- Are you all right?
- Doctor, what's wrong with me?

385
00:23:37,682 --> 00:23:38,784
It's all right.

386
00:23:38,917 --> 00:23:41,286
Anyway, let's buy you
some underpants at the shop.

387
00:23:41,353 --> 00:23:43,054
- Go buy some.
- Okay.

388
00:23:43,121 --> 00:23:44,823
Let's go to the restroom. Up we go.

389
00:23:45,457 --> 00:23:46,558
There.

390
00:23:46,725 --> 00:23:48,727
You want to take this? Okay.

391
00:23:50,362 --> 00:23:55,600
If we can't hold a press conference,
is there anything else we can do?

392
00:23:56,468 --> 00:23:57,769
Never give up!

393
00:23:58,336 --> 00:24:03,275
Isn't there anything impressive
we can do that says,

394
00:24:03,575 --> 00:24:06,545
"Hospital Director Shigekatsu Hiruma
is the boss"?

395
00:24:06,611 --> 00:24:07,779
- Yes, there is!
- There is?

396
00:24:08,046 --> 00:24:09,281
A miracle plan!

397
00:24:09,347 --> 00:24:12,150
- There is?
- We'll do it!

398
00:24:12,250 --> 00:24:14,319
- Do what?
- Mr. Yokkaichi's surgery.

399
00:24:15,187 --> 00:24:18,356
And we'll cure him completely
just like he wants!

400
00:24:20,158 --> 00:24:22,093
You're such an idiot.

401
00:24:23,028 --> 00:24:27,299
Here at Totei University Hospital,
there isn't any doctor who could...

402
00:24:31,036 --> 00:24:34,005
Are you talking about Michiko Daimon?

403
00:24:34,072 --> 00:24:35,240
That's right!

404
00:24:35,774 --> 00:24:39,478
Daimon is sure to have
more knowledge than that AI!

405
00:24:39,744 --> 00:24:41,646
- Oh, that's right.
- Yes.

406
00:24:42,147 --> 00:24:43,615
We have

407
00:24:43,715 --> 00:24:48,086
the ultimate weapon of
Michiko Daimon, don't we?

408
00:24:49,354 --> 00:24:50,489
Oh, that's right.

409
00:24:50,589 --> 00:24:52,591
- Get Daimon right away.
- Yes, sir!

410
00:24:54,559 --> 00:24:55,760
- Director Hiruma!
- Yes?

411
00:24:55,827 --> 00:24:58,263
- Dr. Daimon is operating.
- What?

412
00:24:58,330 --> 00:25:00,131
I knew Dr. Daimon could do it!

413
00:25:03,535 --> 00:25:06,071
What the heck are you doing,
Michiko Daimon?

414
00:25:11,343 --> 00:25:13,411
Stop right now!
Mr. Yokkaichi is my patient.

415
00:25:13,778 --> 00:25:15,347
Yes, that's right.

416
00:25:15,747 --> 00:25:17,349
Then what are you doing?

417
00:25:20,519 --> 00:25:21,753
Mom!

418
00:25:23,388 --> 00:25:24,222
Here.

419
00:25:24,856 --> 00:25:28,460
What the heck are you doing?
My mom has Alzheimer's!

420
00:25:28,660 --> 00:25:31,296
Operating won't cure her!
Are you trying to kill her?

421
00:25:32,397 --> 00:25:34,032
It's not that you can't cure her,

422
00:25:34,499 --> 00:25:36,401
it's that you don't want to
cure her, right?

423
00:25:36,801 --> 00:25:39,337
I told you! She has Alzheimer's!

424
00:25:40,205 --> 00:25:42,674
Good afternoon.
She doesn't have Alzheimer's.

425
00:25:43,441 --> 00:25:46,044
- What?
- Gait disorder.

426
00:25:47,612 --> 00:25:49,047
Dementia.

427
00:25:49,114 --> 00:25:50,649
Who are you?

428
00:25:50,982 --> 00:25:52,050
Urinary incontinence.

429
00:25:52,117 --> 00:25:53,552
What's wrong with me?

430
00:25:54,719 --> 00:25:58,690
Each of these three symptoms
was progressively worsening.

431
00:25:59,424 --> 00:26:00,559
And...

432
00:26:00,659 --> 00:26:03,595
At the end of the hall, turn left.

433
00:26:04,729 --> 00:26:06,831
I finally made it.

434
00:26:07,132 --> 00:26:09,601
She hadn't lost her sense of direction,

435
00:26:10,068 --> 00:26:14,272
so Daimon realized that your mother
didn't have Alzheimer's

436
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:18,143
but idiopathic
normal pressure hydrocephalus.

437
00:26:18,543 --> 00:26:20,111
Hydrocephalus?

438
00:26:20,545 --> 00:26:24,683
But the AI said with 85-percent
probability that she has Alzheimer's.

439
00:26:24,749 --> 00:26:28,386
But that wasn't it. This was within
that three-percent probability.

440
00:26:28,486 --> 00:26:31,590
<i>Others, three percent.
That is my diagnosis.</i>

441
00:26:37,963 --> 00:26:38,797
Here.

442
00:26:39,564 --> 00:26:41,800
LUMBAR SPINE

443
00:26:42,434 --> 00:26:43,802
- Kin, hold this.
- Okay.

444
00:26:44,235 --> 00:26:45,804
- Hypodermic tubing. Kelly clamp.
- Here.

445
00:26:46,605 --> 00:26:48,673
For idiopathic normal
pressure hydrocephalus,

446
00:26:48,773 --> 00:26:51,743
a catheter is inserted in
a cerebrospinal shunt operation

447
00:26:51,810 --> 00:26:53,311
to improve the flow of

448
00:26:53,378 --> 00:26:55,580
excessive cerebrospinal fluid
in the cerebral ventricle

449
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:57,515
and dramatically reduce the symptoms.

450
00:27:05,156 --> 00:27:06,257
We're done.

451
00:27:14,065 --> 00:27:16,234
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

452
00:27:17,469 --> 00:27:18,703
Bye.

453
00:27:22,707 --> 00:27:26,711
Isn't it Mr. Yokkaichi's knee?
That's not the knee.

454
00:27:27,612 --> 00:27:30,348
Daimon's operating on a different patient.

455
00:27:33,151 --> 00:27:35,220
How dare you go and do that to my mother?

456
00:27:35,487 --> 00:27:38,156
This happened because
you don't care about your patients.

457
00:27:38,356 --> 00:27:41,159
- What?
- All you care about is the AI,

458
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:43,762
so you can't heal what can be healed.

459
00:27:46,531 --> 00:27:49,200
Why don't you use your own head some more?

460
00:28:04,215 --> 00:28:05,483
Mom.

461
00:28:07,252 --> 00:28:08,553
I'm sorry.

462
00:28:15,393 --> 00:28:18,029
Why don't you use your own head some more?

463
00:28:20,699 --> 00:28:21,866
Darn her!

464
00:28:26,204 --> 00:28:30,575
HIDEKI KAJI
KAZUMA USHIO

465
00:28:48,326 --> 00:28:51,696
HANG IN THERE, MR. YOKKAICHI!
DON'T LET THAT INJURY GET YOU DOWN!

466
00:28:53,932 --> 00:28:56,701
HOPE YOU GET BETTER SOON!
HURRY BACK AS SOON AS YOU CAN!

467
00:28:56,801 --> 00:28:59,370
I LOVE YOU, MR. YOKKAICHI!
DON'T LET YOUR INJURY GET YOU DOWN

468
00:28:59,437 --> 00:29:01,973
WE'RE WITH YOU ALL THE WAY!
YOU'RE SURE TO BE BACK!

469
00:29:44,415 --> 00:29:45,383
Dr. Daimon!

470
00:29:47,619 --> 00:29:50,622
I figured out a different operation than
the AI's idea for Mr. Yokkaichi.

471
00:29:51,389 --> 00:29:53,391
Autologous cultured cartilage graft.

472
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:56,394
This way, the patient may still
have a future as an athlete.

473
00:29:56,995 --> 00:29:59,230
- Yes, you're right.
- What?

474
00:30:00,064 --> 00:30:02,500
You mean you knew about autologous
cultured cartilage graft?

475
00:30:03,034 --> 00:30:04,369
That's it!

476
00:30:06,404 --> 00:30:09,174
There's still one problem.

477
00:30:09,541 --> 00:30:12,243
What problem?

478
00:30:13,912 --> 00:30:14,813
NURSE
KANA IINO

479
00:30:14,879 --> 00:30:16,981
You don't have Dr. Ushio's permission.

480
00:30:17,048 --> 00:30:19,417
I don't need permission!
I'm checking out of here!

481
00:30:19,584 --> 00:30:22,420
- I'm sorry, but--
- Oh, excuse me.

482
00:30:22,620 --> 00:30:25,690
Mr. Yokkaichi, if you leave,
where will you go?

483
00:30:27,292 --> 00:30:32,130
You see, the only place
that can cure your disease

484
00:30:32,230 --> 00:30:34,232
is here, Totei University Hospital.

485
00:30:34,566 --> 00:30:39,470
I am Mr. Hiruma,
Totei University Hospital Director.

486
00:30:39,604 --> 00:30:41,439
I'm the former director, Mr. Ebina.

487
00:30:41,506 --> 00:30:42,841
Who cares about you.

488
00:30:42,974 --> 00:30:48,279
Mr. Yokkaichi,
as for your future as an athlete,

489
00:30:48,479 --> 00:30:52,116
we at Totei University Hospital will
secure it properly.

490
00:30:52,617 --> 00:30:55,153
- How?
- "How?"

491
00:30:55,653 --> 00:30:56,654
Well, you see...

492
00:30:57,789 --> 00:31:01,526
Dr. Ushio, your timing is perfect.
You see,

493
00:31:02,193 --> 00:31:05,263
I'd like you to explain
to Mr. Yokkaichi yourself

494
00:31:05,330 --> 00:31:08,366
the treatment
that you're going to use on him.

495
00:31:09,100 --> 00:31:10,668
What?

496
00:31:10,768 --> 00:31:12,737
The autologous cultured cartilage graft.

497
00:31:13,104 --> 00:31:14,372
Go ahead.

498
00:31:19,644 --> 00:31:22,614
First, when we remove the tumor,

499
00:31:22,780 --> 00:31:26,217
we'll extract some cartilage tissue
from another part of your body

500
00:31:26,384 --> 00:31:28,219
and cultivate the cartilage cells.

501
00:31:28,319 --> 00:31:30,588
Later, we'll transplant
the cultured cartilage

502
00:31:30,655 --> 00:31:32,390
to where you lost cartilage

503
00:31:32,490 --> 00:31:34,292
and repair your knee cartilage.

504
00:31:35,593 --> 00:31:39,163
Will I be able to run again?

505
00:31:39,797 --> 00:31:44,569
Yes. There is the possibility
you can return as an athlete.

506
00:31:48,106 --> 00:31:49,807
After a very thorough examination,

507
00:31:50,108 --> 00:31:51,709
I found a method

508
00:31:52,377 --> 00:31:56,180
that treats your tumor while
maintaining your knee's function as well.

509
00:31:57,282 --> 00:31:58,750
This won't be a problem at all.

510
00:32:01,686 --> 00:32:03,454
Will you please undergo this surgery?

511
00:32:06,024 --> 00:32:07,592
Yes, please do it.

512
00:32:09,060 --> 00:32:10,161
That's great!

513
00:32:11,462 --> 00:32:13,665
- Magnificent!
- Let's take a photo.

514
00:32:13,731 --> 00:32:14,766
Good idea.

515
00:32:15,099 --> 00:32:16,768
Mr. Yokkaichi, can you take a step back?

516
00:32:17,001 --> 00:32:18,603
- Step back.
- You're in the middle, Director.

517
00:32:18,670 --> 00:32:21,439
- Me? All right.
- Mr. Ushio, stand next to him.

518
00:32:22,040 --> 00:32:23,274
Okay, here goes.

519
00:32:24,475 --> 00:32:26,377
Say cheese!

520
00:32:27,378 --> 00:32:28,579
Nice one!

521
00:32:30,481 --> 00:32:32,150
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

522
00:32:32,250 --> 00:32:35,486
We will now conduct an autologous
cultured cartilage graft

523
00:32:35,820 --> 00:32:39,657
and a right knee
synovial sarcoma excision.

524
00:32:40,224 --> 00:32:41,526
Let us begin.

525
00:32:41,693 --> 00:32:43,094
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

526
00:32:43,161 --> 00:32:47,432
Vitals. BP, 105 over 74. Pulse, 65, sinus.

527
00:32:48,499 --> 00:32:49,734
- Scalpel.
- Here.

528
00:32:59,777 --> 00:33:00,611
Here.

529
00:33:00,678 --> 00:33:01,779
- Four-prong retractor.
- Here.

530
00:33:03,281 --> 00:33:04,716
Dr. Ushio aims to save

531
00:33:04,782 --> 00:33:08,319
the patient's life
as well as his life as an athlete.

532
00:33:09,153 --> 00:33:11,055
Isn't that magnificent?

533
00:33:11,289 --> 00:33:14,359
This case isn't in the AI's data set.

534
00:33:14,692 --> 00:33:17,161
He's creating the first case in the world.

535
00:33:17,762 --> 00:33:18,730
That's right.

536
00:33:19,464 --> 00:33:23,401
This is a tremendous business opportunity.

537
00:33:32,377 --> 00:33:34,746
Incision into the internal
articular capsule complete.

538
00:33:35,279 --> 00:33:39,117
I'll shift the patella outside
and expose the knee joint.

539
00:33:39,951 --> 00:33:40,785
Here.

540
00:33:44,122 --> 00:33:46,391
It's time to excise the synovial sarcoma.

541
00:33:52,397 --> 00:33:54,599
The tumor has spread
farther than expected.

542
00:33:55,400 --> 00:33:56,701
It's quite deep.

543
00:34:06,644 --> 00:34:08,112
Dr. Ushio?

544
00:34:08,980 --> 00:34:10,314
What's the matter?

545
00:34:15,386 --> 00:34:16,788
I can't do this.

546
00:34:29,200 --> 00:34:31,002
What's your problem, Kazuma?

547
00:34:31,636 --> 00:34:32,770
Mom!

548
00:34:33,304 --> 00:34:34,405
Why are you here?

549
00:34:34,672 --> 00:34:37,275
You've been hopeless
since you were a child!

550
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:40,611
You always lose your nerve
at the crucial moment!

551
00:34:42,447 --> 00:34:43,681
Is that right?

552
00:34:44,282 --> 00:34:46,284
Pull yourself together!

553
00:34:47,452 --> 00:34:48,820
Get to it right now!

554
00:34:50,054 --> 00:34:52,356
I will! I tell you.

555
00:34:52,657 --> 00:34:53,791
- Pean forceps.
- Here.

556
00:35:04,735 --> 00:35:06,270
You idiot!

557
00:35:06,337 --> 00:35:09,340
- You're rushing me, Mom!
- Stop the hemorrhaging!

558
00:35:09,740 --> 00:35:11,242
Apply gauze to stop it!

559
00:35:11,342 --> 00:35:13,678
We'll find the source
and repair the vessel!

560
00:35:15,680 --> 00:35:19,317
BP has fallen to 70.
What will you do, lead surgeon?

561
00:35:20,118 --> 00:35:21,352
More gauze! Now!

562
00:35:22,620 --> 00:35:23,788
It won't stop!

563
00:35:27,358 --> 00:35:28,659
Dr. Daimon?

564
00:35:29,260 --> 00:35:31,729
I told you there was still a problem.

565
00:35:32,196 --> 00:35:33,531
What's the problem?

566
00:35:33,598 --> 00:35:36,200
The problem is your ability.

567
00:35:38,803 --> 00:35:40,438
Out of the way!

568
00:35:42,340 --> 00:35:43,741
Popliteal artery damaged.

569
00:35:43,808 --> 00:35:46,010
We'll stop the hemorrhaging with
a sterile tourniquet.

570
00:35:46,077 --> 00:35:49,213
Lead surgeon,
don't just stand there. Help out!

571
00:35:49,413 --> 00:35:50,381
Right.

572
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:53,251
We'll extend the incision
and approach from there.

573
00:35:53,317 --> 00:35:54,285
- Scalpel.
- Here.

574
00:35:58,923 --> 00:36:01,959
SURGERY TIME

575
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:09,367
Damaged location found.
I'll ligate and repair it.

576
00:36:09,433 --> 00:36:11,068
6-0 polypropylene.

577
00:36:20,044 --> 00:36:22,580
He's so pitiful.

578
00:36:35,593 --> 00:36:38,262
I see tumor infiltration at
the rear of the articular capsule.

579
00:36:38,563 --> 00:36:40,198
It has even gotten to there?

580
00:36:40,998 --> 00:36:42,333
We can't go any further.

581
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:44,569
He won't be able to walk, let alone run.

582
00:36:45,369 --> 00:36:48,172
I'll reconstruct the rear articular
capsule with his iliotibial tract.

583
00:36:48,339 --> 00:36:49,373
Hey.

584
00:36:49,674 --> 00:36:53,044
The patient's QOL is priority.
Don't do this, Daimon.

585
00:36:53,244 --> 00:36:54,812
I never fail.

586
00:37:00,718 --> 00:37:02,086
- Size 1 absorbable suture.
- Here.

587
00:37:17,268 --> 00:37:18,436
Amazing.

588
00:37:30,348 --> 00:37:34,285
BP, 110 over 78. Pulse, 66, sinus.

589
00:37:34,752 --> 00:37:35,920
Done.

590
00:37:42,493 --> 00:37:44,729
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

591
00:37:45,062 --> 00:37:46,397
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

592
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:49,800
Magnificent!

593
00:37:52,403 --> 00:37:57,408
Ma'am, Dr. Ushio did a wonderful job.

594
00:37:59,410 --> 00:38:00,745
He did?

595
00:38:02,947 --> 00:38:06,517
Dr. Ushio, please write
a case report right away.

596
00:38:07,151 --> 00:38:09,987
Name it, "Ushio surgical method for

597
00:38:10,054 --> 00:38:12,490
combined autologous
cultured cartilage graft

598
00:38:12,990 --> 00:38:17,228
and synovial sarcoma excision."
This is the world's first case!

599
00:38:18,429 --> 00:38:20,765
The first case in the world?

600
00:38:27,438 --> 00:38:28,706
Yes, sir.

601
00:38:33,010 --> 00:38:36,013
- Yes! Well done!
- Bravo!

602
00:38:36,314 --> 00:38:39,784
Thank you so much, Daimon. Thank goodness.

603
00:38:40,351 --> 00:38:41,519
- Ebina.
- Yes?

604
00:38:41,585 --> 00:38:42,586
Okay,

605
00:38:42,653 --> 00:38:45,723
- give this photo to the press.
- Okay.

606
00:38:46,290 --> 00:38:49,527
We'll also hold a press conference,
so please handle that too.

607
00:38:49,593 --> 00:38:51,696
- Yes, sir! Goodbye.
- Okay. Bye.

608
00:38:52,296 --> 00:38:53,764
- Ebina.
- Yes?

609
00:38:54,031 --> 00:38:55,132
Have you been drinking lately?

610
00:38:55,199 --> 00:38:56,667
- No, I quit recently.
- What?

611
00:38:57,134 --> 00:38:58,436
My wife got angry at me.

612
00:39:00,438 --> 00:39:02,239
The surgery was a success.

613
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:09,980
I'll be able to run again, right?

614
00:39:12,116 --> 00:39:15,152
In four weeks,
we'll transplant the cultured cartilage

615
00:39:15,219 --> 00:39:16,687
to the damaged area.

616
00:39:17,488 --> 00:39:20,725
After that, you'll need
a year of physical therapy.

617
00:39:21,425 --> 00:39:22,693
Thank you.

618
00:39:25,696 --> 00:39:27,531
I swear I'll make a comeback.

619
00:39:28,265 --> 00:39:29,767
And I swear I'll get the gold.

620
00:39:30,601 --> 00:39:33,037
Do your best. I'm looking forward to it.

621
00:39:43,314 --> 00:39:46,784
<i>This is the story of
a maverick woman doctor.</i>

622
00:39:47,718 --> 00:39:49,053
Dr. Daimon!

623
00:39:49,453 --> 00:39:52,623
You may think
I owe you something after this.

624
00:39:54,525 --> 00:39:56,293
You're wrong about that.

625
00:39:57,428 --> 00:39:59,029
I'm a director of surgery.

626
00:39:59,363 --> 00:40:01,332
The lower ranks work for their superiors.

627
00:40:01,665 --> 00:40:05,536
That's what an organization is.
Make sure you remember that.

628
00:40:06,036 --> 00:40:07,772
<i>This woman...</i>

629
00:40:08,038 --> 00:40:09,240
I decline.

630
00:40:10,274 --> 00:40:11,709
I'm a part-timer.

631
00:40:15,346 --> 00:40:19,750
<i>She hates groups, hates authority,
and hates restrictions.</i>

632
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:23,654
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

633
00:40:23,821 --> 00:40:25,289
<i>are her weapons.</i>

634
00:40:26,190 --> 00:40:28,192
ASSISTANT HOSPITAL DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

635
00:40:30,528 --> 00:40:31,829
Excuse me.

636
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:35,065
What a nice smell.

637
00:40:37,568 --> 00:40:42,673
I would like to thank you
for employing Daimon and Jonouchi.

638
00:40:43,140 --> 00:40:44,341
This is a melon.

639
00:40:47,645 --> 00:40:49,380
This is the bill.

640
00:40:51,315 --> 00:40:52,850
We didn't use them.

641
00:40:53,117 --> 00:40:56,854
Dr. Daimon did all of it
without our permission.

642
00:40:57,788 --> 00:41:01,659
I don't believe we are obliged
to pay this time.

643
00:41:02,393 --> 00:41:04,061
I doubt that.

644
00:41:04,261 --> 00:41:08,199
After trying to figure out
whether I should submit the bill

645
00:41:08,532 --> 00:41:13,270
to Director Hiruma
or Assistant Director Tange,

646
00:41:18,275 --> 00:41:20,778
I found this.

647
00:41:21,045 --> 00:41:23,447
<i>WEEKLY JAPAN ECONOMICS</i>

648
00:41:24,281 --> 00:41:25,916
What the heck is this?

649
00:41:27,284 --> 00:41:28,719
KIYOAKI YOKKAICHI SAVED BY AI TREATMENT!

650
00:41:29,220 --> 00:41:31,222
How come this isn't me?

651
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:33,457
Why the heck is Tange in here?

652
00:41:35,826 --> 00:41:38,529
That's quite a wonderful photo.

653
00:41:39,363 --> 00:41:41,265
So, I figured

654
00:41:41,365 --> 00:41:44,602
my only choice was to submit
my bill to Assistant Director Tange.

655
00:41:45,236 --> 00:41:46,604
According to that,

656
00:41:46,670 --> 00:41:49,840
even the autologous cultured
cartilage graft

657
00:41:50,274 --> 00:41:53,711
happened according to
the AI's diagnostic program.

658
00:41:54,612 --> 00:41:59,083
The program was developed by
a medical equipment manufacturer

659
00:41:59,183 --> 00:42:04,388
which is invested in by the fund
you run, Assistant Director Tange.

660
00:42:04,788 --> 00:42:09,727
Ultimately, you'll reap
an easy profit from this.

661
00:42:10,294 --> 00:42:16,066
Naturally, only if you shut
the mouths of me and Daimon.

662
00:42:16,433 --> 00:42:20,137
I'm not good at reading
other people's real intentions.

663
00:42:22,306 --> 00:42:23,641
But let this

664
00:42:25,442 --> 00:42:27,511
put an end to this situation.

665
00:42:28,045 --> 00:42:29,647
Understood.

666
00:42:33,784 --> 00:42:35,085
What the heck is this?

667
00:42:35,152 --> 00:42:36,320
Excuse me.

668
00:42:37,788 --> 00:42:39,423
"Two hundred million"?

669
00:42:40,057 --> 00:42:44,328
Oh, dear. I accidentally added a zero.

670
00:42:46,096 --> 00:42:48,832
I guess my age is catching up to me.

671
00:42:56,273 --> 00:42:58,008
Goodbye.

672
00:43:13,891 --> 00:43:16,493
Thank you!

673
00:43:21,265 --> 00:43:25,035
Thank you, Nichotan!

674
00:43:30,708 --> 00:43:32,409
Akira!

675
00:43:33,277 --> 00:43:36,180
We got a present from Mrs. Ushio!

676
00:43:36,246 --> 00:43:38,749
Oh, my! She didn't have to
go to such trouble.

677
00:43:39,316 --> 00:43:42,319
- What is it?
- There we go!

678
00:43:43,354 --> 00:43:44,288
Welsh onions?

679
00:43:46,156 --> 00:43:48,792
There is nothing but Welsh onions in here!

680
00:43:49,026 --> 00:43:51,228
We can eat nothing
but Welsh onions for a month.

681
00:43:52,162 --> 00:43:54,264
- Akira.
- What?

682
00:43:54,331 --> 00:43:56,767
Look what I found!

683
00:43:57,001 --> 00:43:59,336
The mother of a doctor
knows the right thing to do!

684
00:44:00,404 --> 00:44:01,639
I'm so excited!

685
00:44:01,739 --> 00:44:03,307
How much is it?

686
00:44:06,310 --> 00:44:07,478
- There!
- Here, use these.

687
00:44:07,544 --> 00:44:09,179
It's okay.

688
00:44:10,214 --> 00:44:13,083
What's this? She sure is cautious.

689
00:44:13,150 --> 00:44:17,187
- But it's so exciting!
- But it's so exciting!

690
00:44:18,188 --> 00:44:20,391
There's another one!

691
00:44:20,457 --> 00:44:24,294
- But it's so exciting!
- But it's so exciting!

692
00:44:24,361 --> 00:44:27,798
This is the last one. There's another one!

693
00:44:28,399 --> 00:44:30,200
What's with her?

694
00:44:30,801 --> 00:44:33,070
- Yes!
- Nice!

695
00:44:34,638 --> 00:44:36,206
10 PERCENT OFF MEAL COUPON

696
00:44:36,273 --> 00:44:40,611
Discount tickets for restaurants in Gunma?

697
00:44:41,045 --> 00:44:42,479
What?

698
00:44:47,384 --> 00:44:50,087
You must be kidding me, lady!

699
00:44:50,154 --> 00:44:52,556
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

700
00:44:52,790 --> 00:44:56,060
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

701
00:44:57,461 --> 00:44:59,296
<i>It's a pleasure to see you.</i>

702
00:44:59,363 --> 00:45:01,065
- What a rude woman.
- Same to you.

703
00:45:01,165 --> 00:45:02,533
Here, I'm Masa.

704
00:45:02,599 --> 00:45:04,334
<i>Illicit business? That's just wrong!</i>

705
00:45:04,435 --> 00:45:07,037
<i>This is the one thing
I will risk my life to save.</i>

706
00:45:07,104 --> 00:45:09,239
<i>I will protect what's precious to you.</i>

707
00:45:09,406 --> 00:45:11,408
This is a promise between women.
